{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FigureEightCasimirWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FigureEightCasimirWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L164-L169","doc":"Conditional bar symmetry: the first-correction weight is invariant\nunder the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`, consistent with it being a\nfunction of the skein square `h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L158-L162","doc":"Conditional enhancement bound: the weight never falls below `1`\non `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_classical","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L152-L156","doc":"Conditional classical limit: the correction degenerates to weight\n`1` at `q = 1` (no substrate deformation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_taylor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_taylor","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L143-L150","doc":"Conditional Taylor form: the first-correction weight is\n`1 + (3/4)h²` plus an explicit positive `O(h⁴)` remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_eq_jones41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight_eq_jones41","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L137-L137","doc":"the carrier identification: the weight is the Jones polynomial\n(Markov trace) of the figure-eight knot ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.weight","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L134-L134","doc":"relative weight of the first substrate correction, per mode ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.FirstInteractingCasimirCorrection","kind":"class","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L124-L137","doc":"**Conjectural input** (`conj:casimir-first-q-correction`, §3b-cond\npattern). The conjecture: the first substrate-dependent correction to\nthe plate-bounded vacuum mode-sum enters with the Markov-trace weight\nof the minimal hyperbolic braided mode — the figure-eight knot `4₁`.\nThis class axiomatises that identification; the theorems below are\nfully verified consequences, conditional on an instance. No instance\nis provided: constructing one (the interacting-mode mode-sum) is the\nopen content of the conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:casimir-first-q-correction","label":"conj:casimir-first-q-correction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/casimir-first-q-correction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L116-L122","doc":"The weight is bounded below by `1` on `q > 0`: the substrate\ncorrection carried by `4₁` is an enhancement, never a suppression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L107-L114","doc":"Bar symmetry: the figure-eight weight is invariant under the bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹` — it is a function of `h² = (q − q⁻¹)²` alone, as\nthe Taylor form makes explicit. Holds unconditionally (at `q = 0` both\nsides are `1` with the `0⁻¹ = 0` convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_taylor_remainder_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_taylor_remainder_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L99-L105","doc":"The remainder in `jones41_taylor` is nonnegative for `q > 0`: the weight\nis bounded *below* by its second-order Taylor polynomial `1 + (3/4)h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_taylor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_taylor","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L81-L97","doc":"**The result, as a theorem.**  With `h = q − q⁻¹`, the figure-eight Jones\nweight expands as\n  `J_{4_1}(q) = 1 + (3/4)·h² + R(q)`,\nwhere the remainder `R(q) = h⁴ / (4·(h² + 8 + 4(q+q⁻¹)))` is *exact*, and for\n`q > 0` is positive and of order `h⁴` (its denominator `→ 64` as `q → 1`).\nThe leading coefficient `3/4` is forced by `ring`; it is not a fitted constant.\nThis is the precise sense in which \"`J_{4_1} = 1 + (3/4)h² + O(h⁴)`\" holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_three_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_three_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L73-L79","doc":"Division form on `q > 0`: `4(J−1) − 3h² = h⁴ / (positive)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_remainder_denom_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_remainder_denom_pos","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L65-L71","doc":"The remainder denominator is strictly positive for `q > 0`, so the\n`O(h⁴)` remainder `h⁴ / (·)` is genuinely small and sign-definite: the\nleading `h²` coefficient of `J_{4_1} − 1` is exactly `3/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_three_quarters_cleared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_three_quarters_cleared","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**The 3/4 is exact.** Cleared form of\n`J_{4_1} = 1 + (3/4) h² + O(h⁴)`: the residual `4(J−1) − 3h²`, times the\nexplicit remainder denominator, equals exactly `h⁴`. Proof is `ring` after\nclearing `q⁻¹` (needs only `q ≠ 0`) — there is no fitted constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.sSq_sub_hSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.sSq_sub_hSq","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L50-L53","doc":"`s² − h² = 4`, with `s = q+q⁻¹`, `h = q−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_eq_sform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_eq_sform","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L45-L48","doc":"`s`-form: `J_{4_1} = (q+q⁻¹)² − (q+q⁻¹) − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41_one","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L42-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.jones41","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/FigureEightCasimirWeight.lean#L38-L40","doc":"Jones polynomial of the figure-eight knot `4_1`, in the skein\nvariable `q`, normalised so `jones41 1 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}